[{:db/id 17592186133841 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ffe5914e-4912-5ff3-9b15-3a1462960003"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133840 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3676ec52-02c6-5b83-a547-e552c5ceb042"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3676ec52-02c6-5b83-a547-e552c5ceb042" :question/id #uuid "3676ec52-02c6-5b83-a547-e552c5ceb042" :question/math-academy-id "q-81338" :question/problem "![](images/41/4121d975786de30f34e493e7ac49e5cdc8e66621e800321008ba4ba501fb818f.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $y=-{x}^{2},$ and $y=-1,$ as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}({x}^{2}y-3x)\\,dA=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are \n$-1\\le x\\le 1.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](images/ef/ef6450f795d0edea8a3217e28d7f1a966d5b1c62f9241826213de0485af5f860.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le -{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}y-3x)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{-{x}^{2}}({x}^{2}y-3x)\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3df51106-2408-5663-8451-c957471724da"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3df51106-2408-5663-8451-c957471724da" :answer-field/id #uuid "3df51106-2408-5663-8451-c957471724da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-93b1f2e7-cf7b-5b8a-b5bb-c62e89e19fa2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-58f2f8c3-eca9-558a-ae7f-9a78208457ea" "answer-93b1f2e7-cf7b-5b8a-b5bb-c62e89e19fa2" "answer-ef3be0a4-83b9-54e6-81b8-88c21e425fc7" "answer-647e13d7-fe24-5171-9f25-59459873bf42" "answer-93175eb3-2514-5cc0-a423-e088c96ac28d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58f2f8c3-eca9-558a-ae7f-9a78208457ea" :answer/id #uuid "58f2f8c3-eca9-558a-ae7f-9a78208457ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{-{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{2}y-3x)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93b1f2e7-cf7b-5b8a-b5bb-c62e89e19fa2" :answer/id #uuid "93b1f2e7-cf7b-5b8a-b5bb-c62e89e19fa2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{-{x}^{2}}({x}^{2}y-3x)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef3be0a4-83b9-54e6-81b8-88c21e425fc7" :answer/id #uuid "ef3be0a4-83b9-54e6-81b8-88c21e425fc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-{x}^{2}}^{-1}({x}^{2}y-3x)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-647e13d7-fe24-5171-9f25-59459873bf42" :answer/id #uuid "647e13d7-fe24-5171-9f25-59459873bf42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-{x}^{2}}^{-1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}y-3x)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93175eb3-2514-5cc0-a423-e088c96ac28d" :answer/id #uuid "93175eb3-2514-5cc0-a423-e088c96ac28d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{-{x}^{2}}({x}^{2}y-3x)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ffe5914e-4912-5ff3-9b15-3a1462960003" :question/id #uuid "ffe5914e-4912-5ff3-9b15-3a1462960003" :question/math-academy-id "q-132285" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}({x}^{2}+2y)\\,dy\\,dx=$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}({x}^{2}+2y)\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}({x}^{2}+2y)\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}]_{{x}^{2}}^{1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+1-{x}^{4}-{x}^{4})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+1-2{x}^{4})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+1-2{x}^{4})\\,dx & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x-\\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+1-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-85ef2574-1c06-549a-a456-4b22b82491c8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-85ef2574-1c06-549a-a456-4b22b82491c8" :answer-field/id #uuid "85ef2574-1c06-549a-a456-4b22b82491c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3aabdbf2-aad9-5028-8b69-34e437771408" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1377aca7-a017-58fe-8e23-256c042e11b6" "answer-100fac5f-cc12-56dc-9567-ee01010ba781" "answer-3aabdbf2-aad9-5028-8b69-34e437771408" "answer-41ea5617-4c16-5bdc-a231-c9432f86dc81" "answer-93d7f804-0816-5794-84e7-a2fe566f8c71"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1377aca7-a017-58fe-8e23-256c042e11b6" :answer/id #uuid "1377aca7-a017-58fe-8e23-256c042e11b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-100fac5f-cc12-56dc-9567-ee01010ba781" :answer/id #uuid "100fac5f-cc12-56dc-9567-ee01010ba781" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3aabdbf2-aad9-5028-8b69-34e437771408" :answer/id #uuid "3aabdbf2-aad9-5028-8b69-34e437771408" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41ea5617-4c16-5bdc-a231-c9432f86dc81" :answer/id #uuid "41ea5617-4c16-5bdc-a231-c9432f86dc81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{18}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93d7f